      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CATCH THE RED EYE (1) dug deep to score by a neck at Pinjarra last start at her first run back from a spell. The inside draw should ensure a cosy run. Tackles a stronger assignment but should be fitter so can make it two for two this time in work. SUN PUBLISHER NZ (10) cruised home by 17m the last time he raced here last month to maintain a perfect record at this circuit and distance. Has placed in two of three outings since. Tricky draw but he is going well. FLOAT MY BOAT (8) may need some luck from the back row but is looming as a real threat after a good effort last start, held up before finishing second at Gloucester Park. FOLLOW ROCKNROLL (9) continues a run of second line draws but owns a good record at this circuit and distance so could measure up here.",
